 The woman herself is spoken once and heard at every depth.
 In the garden she is Eve; but Scripture will not leave her one woman.
 Isaiah watches the same mother travail: __“before her pain came, she was delivered of a *man child*… for as soon as *Zion* travailed, she brought forth her children”__ (Isaiah 66:7-8) — the woman who bears the man child is Zion, the covenant people, pictured everywhere in the prophets as a woman, a bride, a mother.
